Opcodes.json is the SM83 (Game Boy CPU) opcode table from gbdev's gb-opcodes:

  repository: https://github.com/gbdev/gb-opcodes
  file:       https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gbdev/gb-opcodes/376f61c86fdac2048f7ce5fe838ae756b306017e/Opcodes.json
  commit:     376f61c86fdac2048f7ce5fe838ae756b306017e (2024-12-13, the latest commit touching Opcodes.json)
  fetched:    2026-11-06
  license:    CC0-1.0 (LICENSE, copied from the same commit)

It is committed unmodified. scripts/disasm/gen_opcodes.py generates
crates/engine/src/disasm/table.rs from it, and
crates/engine/tests/it/disasm_table.rs checks the disassembler against it for all
512 opcodes. Cycles are T-cycles at single speed; a second figure is the
not-taken cost of a conditional branch.
